    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hi, i'm a bit overwhelmed with the visa situation for an upcoming engineering team trip through SE Asia. we're hitting multiple countries like vietnam, thailand, and indonesia. i'm really struggling to distinguish when we need a full entry visa vs just a transit visa for laying over in certain hubs. can you give me a basic checklist or breakdown of what we need to look out for so nobody gets stuck at customs? thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I can help you with that. A transit visa is usually required to leave the airport and enter another country for a limited time, while a full entry visa allows you to stay in a country for an extended period. Here's a simple checklist for your team trip: \n\n- Check if any of the countries you'll be visiting require a full entry visa for all nationalities. Some countries, like Indonesia, only require a visa on arrival (VOA), but may require one for Schengen Area countries.\n- Look up the specific requirements for your team's nationality, as requirements can vary greatly.\n- Check the length of time you'll be staying in each country and the length of time allowed on a transit visa to ensure you're meeting the necessary requirements.\n- Always research the visa requirements for each country and hotel or accommodation to avoid any issues at customs or entry points.",
